<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. The unaudited financial  results of The Andhra Sugars Limited (  the Holding Company ), its Subsidiaries and Associate (together referred to as  the Group ) have been prepared in accordance with the Indian Accounting Standards (Ind AS) as prescribed under section 133 of the Companies Act 2013 read with the Companies (Indian Accounting Standard) Rules, 2015 (as amended).   2. The figures of the Fourth Quarter  for Consolidated  Operations are the balancing figures between audited figures in respect of full financial year upto 31st March, 2024 and un-audited year to date figures upto the third quarter ended 31st December, 2023 which were subjected to limited review.   3. The total exceptional item for the quarter and Year ended 31st March, 2024 includes Rs.235.77 lakhs is towards provision for Impairment of assets in Sugar Unit at Bhimadole and Rs. 259.01 lakhs is towards provision for impairment of assets in Power Generation unit at Tanuku.   4.Decrease in Profit and Turnover is mainly on account of decrease in the Selling Prices of Chlor-Alkali (Caustic Soda and its Bye-Products) and Chemicals.   5.Other Income for the quarter ended June 30th, 2024 includes Rs. 1178.59 lakhs towards sale of Scrap and Rs. 561.73 lakhs towards Dividend from the Associate in respect of Parent Company.   6.During the Financial Year 2019-20, the Associate Company (APL) has initiated the process of renewal of the Land Lease on which the plant is located with Visakhapatnam Port Trust (VPT) for a further period of 30 years with effect from 27.06.2019.  APL has submitted its Technical &amp; Financial Bid against the tender floated by VPT. As APL was the sole bidder for the Tender, VPT accepted both Technical Bid &amp; Financial Bid.  Later -on, VPT has cancelled the tender and issued re-tender.  Aggrieved by the action of VPT, APL has filed a writ petition under Article 226 before the Hon’ble High Court of Andhra Pradesh.   The Hon’ble High Court of Andhra Pradesh has allowed the writ Petition filed by the APL seeking the cancellation of the order dated 18.08.2020, cancelling the tender notification dated 07.08.2019 and fresh tender notification dated 24.08.2020 issued by VPT towards the lease of the land and directed VPT to execute the lease deed, vide its order dated 25th February 2022. Further, on 19th March 2022, APL has written a letter to the Chief Engineer, VPT requesting him to kindly finalise the land lease deed and fix-up the date for execution of the said lease deed.  VPT has preferred an appeal against the Hon’ble High Court of Andhra Pradesh order dated 25.02.2022 before division bench of Hon’ble High Court of Andhra Pradesh and the same is pending.   7.The above unaudited financial results of the Group have been reviewed by  the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at their respective Meetings held on 12.08.2024 and statutory auditors have carried out the limited review.   8.Previous period figures have been re-grouped wherever necessary to conform the current period presentation.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
